        {
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "text": "Suspense ",
          "italic": true
        },
        {
          "text": "is an AVAnnotate project that explores how suspense is created through audiovisual form in D. W. Griffith’s 1909 film The Lonely Villa. Using time-based annotations, the project draws attention to specific moments in the film and examines how techniques such as editing, pacing, performance, framing, and music contribute to the development of tension. "
        },
        {
          "text": "Rather ",
          "bold": true,
          "underline": true,
          "highlight": "#e15b5b"
        },
        {
          "text": "than simply presenting the film, the project uses annotation to encourage close audiovisual analysis, allowing viewers to move between the film itself and commentary on how suspense is constructed."
        }
      ]
